# Code owners for release-automation.
#
# Enforced by the `main` ruleset, which has require_code_owner_review enabled:
# every PR needs an approving review from an owner of each path it touches.
#
# Notes on syntax, matching the conventions in paritytech/polkadot-sdk:
#
#   - The latest matching rule wins, so the specific paths below override `*`.
#   - Multiple owners on one path are OR, not AND: any one of them satisfies the
#     review requirement.
#   - An owner needs write access or better. A team with read access is silently
#     ignored, with no error. @paritytech/engineering has read access to this
#     repo and must not be listed here.

# Shared ownership of the repo: either Release Engineering or CI can review.
# This also covers CODEOWNERS itself, so the gate cannot be quietly removed.
*                        @paritytech/release-engineering @paritytech/ci

# The guard decides whether a ref may be built at all, and its logic is
# deliberately NOT sourced from the repository it verifies: a crafted tag could
# otherwise supply a validator that returns success. Kept with Release
# Engineering alone so changes to the gate are reviewed by its owners.
# See paritytech/release-engineering#310 and #314.
/.github/scripts/guard/  @paritytech/release-engineering
